s included.\n\nLet's code.\n\nWe'll write Python code inside the solve function.\n\nPotential pitfalls: The case payload might have nodes with missing parent? But root has parent null.\n\nWe'll use recursion or loop to propagate.\n\nWrite:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\n    id2node = {node['id']: node for node in nodes}\n    # find root\n    root_id = next(node['id'] for node in nodes if node['parent'] is None)\n    retained = set()\n    retained.add(root_id)\n    # propagate up\n    def mark_ancestors(node_id):\n        while node_id in id2node:\n            retained.add(node_id)\n            node_id = id2node[node_id]['parent']\n            if node_id is None:\n                break\n    # Mark all non-removable nodes\n    for node in nodes:\n        if not node['removable']:\n            mark_ancestors(node['id'])\n    # Check coverage for required symbols\n    # Build set of symbols currently covered\n    covered_symbols = set()\n    for nid in retained:\n        covered_symbols.add(id2node[nid]['symbol'])\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym in covered_symbols:\n            continue\n        # Find candidate nodes with this symbol\n        candidates = [node for node in nodes if node['symbol'] == sym and node['id'] not in retained]\n        if not candidates:\n            # If no candidate, we must use a node already retained? But that contradicts covered_symbols check. Possibly the symbol is only in retained nodes? Already covered. So this should not happen.\n            continue\n        # Choose the one with highest utility (max)\n        best = max(candidates, key=lambda n: n['utility'])\n        mark_ancestors(best['id'])\n        # Update covered symbols after adding\n        # But we can just recompute later; but for simplicity, we can add the new node's symbol and its ancestors' symbols.\n        # Actually, adding best may also add ancestors with symbols that might cover oth